# Citation metadata for GitHub's "Cite this repository" button.
#
# GitHub renders `preferred-citation` when it is present, so that block is
# the arXiv paper and must match the BibTeX in both README halves;
# tests/test_citation_metadata.py holds the three copies together, and the
# software metadata below to pyproject.toml.
# `repository-code` stays at the top level only: ruby-cff, the library GitHub
# Docs names, prefers it over `url` for the BibTeX link, so inside
# `preferred-citation` it would replace the arXiv link with the repository
# link.
# There is deliberately no `version` or `date-released`: this file is not
# one of the version pins bumped at release time, and a stale version is
# worse than none.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenAI4S in your research, please cite the paper below.
type: software
title: OpenAI4S
abstract: >-
  A pure-stdlib hybrid Code-as-Action scientific research agent.
